<header><p class="st-kicker">republic · Poland, Lithuania and Russia</p><h1 class="st-title">Don Republic</h1><p class="st-meta">1918 CE – 1920 CE · capital Novocherkassk</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">The anti-Bolshevik state of the Don Cossacks in the Russian Civil War, led by Ataman Krasnov and later part of Denikin's White movement.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p>After Ataman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexey-kaledin">Alexey Kaledin</a> shot himself in February 1918 as Bolsheviks overran the Don, a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> uprising in spring drove them out. In May 1918 a Cossack assembly in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novocherkassk">Novocherkassk</a> elected General <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-krasnov">Pyotr Krasnov</a> ataman and proclaimed the independent Almighty Don Host, heir to the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/don-cossack-host">Don Cossack Host</a>.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pyotr-krasnov">Krasnov</a> allied with <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/germany">Germany</a>, from which he obtained weapons, and organised a sizeable Don army that besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volgograd">Tsaritsyn</a> in 1918. The republic had a constitution, its own currency and a government based on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/cossacks">Cossack</a> institutions. After Germany's defeat Krasnov resigned in February 1919, and under Ataman <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afrikan-bogaevsky">Afrikan Bogaevsky</a> the Don joined <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/anton-denikin">Denikin</a>'s <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/armed-forces-of-south-russia">Armed Forces of South Russia</a>.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>The White advance on <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/moscow">Moscow</a> failed in 1919. The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/red-army">Red Army</a> captured <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/novocherkassk">Novocherkassk</a> in January 1920, and the Don was absorbed into the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/empire/russian-sfsr">Russian SFSR</a>. The Bolsheviks' policy of decossackisation brought executions and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deportation">deportations</a>.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><figure class="st-fig"><img src="/images/states/don-republic.jpg" alt="Don Republic" width="320" height="201"><figcaption>Image: Riwnodennyk · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Flag_of_Don_Cossacks.svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">source</a></figcaption></figure><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>1918 CE – 1920 CE</dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>republic</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Novocherkassk</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Alexey Kaledin, Pyotr Krasnov, Afrikan Bogaevsky</dd><dt>Religion</dt><dd>Eastern Orthodox Christianity</dd><dt>Language</dt><dd>Russian</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd>Russia</dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Almighty Don Host</dd></dl></aside></div>
